document: docs/adr/0011-vcs-gov-owns-the-commit-and-merge-request-contract.md
blob: 7499e7993b7629a83bb10a80f5c65e9c133fd3b9
decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: Who owns the commit and MR conventions, and what do projects declare?

Records that vcs-gov owns the commit message format and MR body structure, projects declare only values in the `vcs` block, and a native commit-msg hook enforces it.
Translated from Korean to English; frontmatter, the `vcs.*` keys, commands, `CLAUDE.md §2` and the measured counts (503 commits, 31 = 6.2%, 88 = 17.5%, 110-line hook, 20 recent commits) are unchanged.
Korean literal kept on purpose: `…것` (the forbidden Korean ending), with a short English gloss; `·` lists kept as the literal separator character.
"한국어 명사형" rendered as "Korean noun-form endings"; the Hangul 3-byte / `wc -m` C-locale constraint kept verbatim in meaning.
Headings mapped to Decision, Background and Constraints, Rationale and Alternatives, Consequences.

